WEBVTT

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.150
No fever.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.020
Normal pulse, too.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.650
Then don't tell me...

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:21.520
Did your company go under?!

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:22.770
It did not.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.190
Did you kill some--

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.480
I did not.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.310
Then why would you do something like that?

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:32.020
You mean invite you to my house?

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:35.560
You must have a reason.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:36.850
I felt like it?

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:39.770
Liar!

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:42.150
So, you really just want to hang out?

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:45.560
You never do things
because you "feel like it"!

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:44.020
Yes, really.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:45.560
Great. I'll go.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.770
Okay. When works for you?

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:50.520
How about... Sunday?

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:51.560
Okay!

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:54.100
Now that's settled, time to plan!

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.480
This has gotten fun.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:59.940
Oh, how about I bring something to snack on?

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.270
What would you like?

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:03.600
Yes! I'd like something pricey.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.560
I'm asking Neiru.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:08.440
Maybe I'll bring a <i>takoyaki</i> maker.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:10.150
Forget that junk for now.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:11.150
"Junk"?

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:12.600
Just listen.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.020
Oh, does Sunday work for you?

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:16.060
Oh, that might be nice!

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:16.060
Yeah.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:18.150
Hey, what about you two?

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:19.770
Of course it's fine.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:21.770
I wouldn't miss it.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:34.860
Wonder Egg Priority

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:59.190
This is a recording of
President Aonuma's dreams.

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:01.770
Using the technology developed here,

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:06.740
it is possible to analyze brainwaves
and convert the subject's dreams to video.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:05.410
Episode 9: 'A Story No One Knows'

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:06.990
Whoa.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:08.830
The Boss of Takoyaki

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:08.830
The Boss of Takoyaki

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.940
They're not dreams, though.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.270
But they're not reality either.

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:16.060
Science is amazing.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:18.060
The picture is still rough and monochrome,

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:18.060
Ai, have her record you.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:23.400
but with more research,
it will one day be clear and in full color.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:21.190
We'll get a sexy fantasy out of it.

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:23.400
Don't lump me in with you.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.940
I can't believe you live at your company.

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:27.980
This feels like a field trip.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:30.480
Who are you, anyway, Neiru?

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:32.850
What an existentialist question.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.400
What's that?

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.310
Are you familiar with a group called Plati?

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:42.230
Yes. I heard only people
with really high IQs can join.

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:45.770
Ms. Neiru is a member of Japan Plati.

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:48.900
Wow. I knew you were really smart.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:51.310
I'm just good at thinking logically.

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:53.520
How modest, ma'am.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:57.150
I was born via artificial
insemination of a member.

00:03:57.150 --> 00:04:00.850
Oh, so that's why you said
you never had parents.

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:04.480
For real? They won't tell you
who your parents are?

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:08.230
There'd be no point. It was just a pairing.

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:11.440
That puts my worries in perspective.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.350
We've reached floor B9.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.480
This is our medical floor.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.560
Are you a doctor, too, Neiru?

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:24.520
No. I'm not in charge of this floor.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:26.690
I'm just filling in for now.

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:29.850
Hey, are we there yet?

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:30.580
Here.

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:31.980
Whoa.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:34.060
Well then, excuse me.

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:35.440
Yes. Thank you.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:37.270
Thank you very much.

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:40.350
All right! This is your room, Neiru?

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:40.350
Thank you very much.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.940
Whoa, books galore.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.850
Hey, Neiru,

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:50.520
what's this guy's name?

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:51.810
Adam.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.270
Can I touch him?

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:54.100
Sure.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.480
Clean up all this paper.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:57.850
Come here.

00:04:57.850 --> 00:04:59.560
Where should we eat?

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:02.350
Oh, wait a moment.

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:05.600
I've got exams next week.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:08.020
I haven't studied at all.

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:09.730
Me, too.

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:11.850
You're lucky, Neiru.

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:15.150
You get to run this huge company.

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:18.980
It's like we live in different worlds.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:20.400
I...

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:23.940
Anyway, Rika, isn't it about time?

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:28.230
All right, let's get started!

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:37.940
Yesterday, Rika and I got worked up
talking about fun things to do.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:40.150
It's a pretty color.

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:41.770
Well?

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:43.310
Grown-up, right?

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:46.310
We thought we could all do our nails and stuff.

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:47.480
Ever painted them?

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:48.810
I'll do Neiru's.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:48.780
Nope.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:49.980
Show me your hands.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:49.980
No.

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:54.060
Don't worry. I won't screw up!

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:51.650
You have pretty nails.

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:54.060
Huh? Do I really?

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:58.900
You're good, Momo.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:00.480
You could go pro.

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:01.770
I wonder.

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:04.940
But I think I'd like to be a dietitian.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:07.310
I'm thinking of going to school for it.

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:10.730
Wow. I'm impressed you're
thinking about that stuff.

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:13.310
I want to go abroad.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.600
Wouldn't working in English be cool?

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.060
Then an international marriage to a hot guy.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:19.850
What a surprise.

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:22.190
I wonder where I want to go.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:25.150
Hang on, we're not talking about vacation.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:28.150
Oh, but I might want to try living on my own.

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:29.520
Oh, I get that.

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:32.100
That's a dream of mine, too.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:33.770
There. All done.

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:38.350
One's a different color.

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:39.650
We match.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:46.310
And you, Neiru?

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:47.810
What's your dream?

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:50.230
Oh, yeah, you haven't told us yet.

00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:53.560
I guess we're all sharing our dreams now.

00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:58.440
I think I'll probably stay like this forever.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:06:59.310
Huh?

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:01.480
Come on, I didn't mean that earlier.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:04.020
You don't have to run a company your whole life.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:06.650
Oh, if you like books, why not become a writer?

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:09.190
Let me introduce a friend.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:11.190
I want you to meet her.

00:07:11.190 --> 00:07:12.770
Your friend?

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:27.770
Someone's inside.

00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:32.150
Kotobuki Awano. She was born
at Japan Plati like I was.

00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:33.560
Kotobuki.

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:35.520
Adam is her pet.

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:36.980
Her hair color...

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:38.810
She's albino.

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:40.600
She's gorgeous.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:44.810
Albinos are said to bring
good fortune to those around them.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:49.940
Kotobuki was always cheerful and optimistic.

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:52.440
She'd tell me to "really enjoy myself."

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:53.650
"Was"?

00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:55.980
Isn't she just sleeping?

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:57.810
She's in a vegetative state.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:58.690
Huh?

00:07:58.690 --> 00:08:01.400
Kotobuki was a doctor of psychiatry.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:04.650
She was scientifically analyzing
the mysteries of life.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:07.440
Death, in particular.

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:12.650
She performed near-death experiments,
and eventually didn't come back.

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:14.350
Near-death experiments...

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:18.900
Scientists try to solve difficult
problems. It's in their nature.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:21.350
She was your friend, wasn't she?

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:24.350
Yes. I met Kotobuki in a dream.

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:25.730
A dream?

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:27.060
An Egg dream.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:31.850
He's incredible.

00:08:31.850 --> 00:08:33.150
Pinky.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:35.600
Is he a type of corn snake?

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:37.690
Who knows?

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:41.690
It's been a long time, Neiru.

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:43.520
Kotobuki...

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:45.150
Is Adam well?

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:47.810
Yes. You look well, too.

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:51.190
I guess. I'm not bored.

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:52.650
Still, I'm glad.

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:55.400
I get a chance to say goodbye to you.

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:57.400
I'd better thank God.

00:08:57.400 --> 00:09:01.150
We're not children of God, remember?

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:04.310
Scientists who can't believe
in God are incompetent.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:08.060
I'm not a scientist at all.

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:09.480
You know that.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:12.230
Of course. Just needling you.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:17.400
You'll protect me, right?

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:23.100
Or do you want me to protect you?

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:25.690
Oh, that's nice. What a lovely weapon.

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:30.350
Let's really enjoy ourselves.

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:34.810
There you are!

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:38.980
Pinky!

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:45.650
What's that? It's hilarious!

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:47.520
Faster! Faster!

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:50.480
They'll catch us if we don't hurry.

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:52.900
Kotobuki, why did you die?

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:55.310
Why couldn't you come back?

00:09:55.310 --> 00:09:57.150
When adrenaline enters the brain,

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:01.100
they say you see a field of flowers
to overcome the fear of death.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:05.310
I wanted to pick one and bring it back to you.

00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:06.940
This isn't funny!

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:08.690
I won't forgive any more jokes.

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:12.060
The me in the world you're in did die.

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:14.400
But that allowed me to experience it.

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:18.100
I was right, Neiru: Parallel worlds do exist!

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:20.940
The possibility of worlds that might have been.

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:24.270
It was your favorite genre of fiction.

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:27.150
Yes! Our parallel selves are alive!

00:10:27.150 --> 00:10:28.730
That's nice,

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:31.020
but I can't see you ever again.

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:34.310
Being satisfied with seeing
each other is so commonplace.

00:10:34.310 --> 00:10:37.310
We're not some couple
that can't handle long-distance.

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:40.230
I can't be so philosophical about it yet.

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:52.980
At stage four Thanato,
there was a sweet smell like honey.

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:56.690
I felt like an insect preyed upon
by a carnivorous plant.

00:10:56.690 --> 00:10:58.690
The temptation of death?

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:00.730
Not so much "temptation."

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:03.100
More like my mind and body were abducted.

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:05.350
Abducted? By what?

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:07.310
By innocent sorrow.

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:10.690
What chatty guinea pigs you are!

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:21.810
Ow. That hurt.

00:11:21.810 --> 00:11:23.020
Where's Pinky?

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:24.730
Back in my pendant.

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:27.520
Don't worry. He'll regenerate soon.

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:28.560
I see.

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:30.230
I won't give up.

00:11:30.230 --> 00:11:33.810
No matter what it takes,
I'll go to the place where you died

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:35.060
and bring your statue back to--

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:38.020
You can't envision dying.

00:11:38.020 --> 00:11:41.440
You can't reach an abstract place.

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:43.730
Then I'll use near-death experiments, too.

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:45.350
Don't be ridiculous.

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:47.650
If you went to that zone, you'd die, too.

00:11:47.650 --> 00:11:50.560
What would happen to me in reality then?

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:54.480
Where did you go?!

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:55.900
You must know.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:58.770
The government will come for my body someday.

00:11:58.770 --> 00:12:01.440
I won't let them do that.

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:03.100
It's just a container.

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:05.850
But I was attached to it in my own way.

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:08.100
I don't want adults touching it.

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:09.350
I know.

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:13.850
Then you must know what I want you to do.

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:14.750
I don't.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:16.270
Stop that.

00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:18.810
I know you're not that dense.

00:12:29.230 --> 00:12:30.690
Why?

00:12:30.690 --> 00:12:34.900
Why are you always so selfish?

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:38.350
In the end, you left me to deal with everything!

00:12:38.350 --> 00:12:42.810
Won't you praise my original research methods?

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:45.810
You don't consider other
people's feelings at all!

00:12:45.810 --> 00:12:47.560
You're used to that.

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:50.850
It's still not normal to just die!

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:53.350
Isn't abnormality more fun?

00:12:53.350 --> 00:12:56.100
It's not fun for me!

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:58.270
Look at your face.

00:12:58.270 --> 00:13:02.230
It's fine. You made new friends, right?

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:03.650
How did...?

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:07.060
You're softer than you used to be.

00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:09.480
But they're not like us.

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:11.650
You made connections with people.

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:14.270
That's a wonderful thing.

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:16.230
Treasure them.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:19.150
You aren't there.

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:22.850
I'll make friends with those girls
in another world-line.

00:13:27.150 --> 00:13:31.230
I finally caught you, you cocky brat.

00:13:31.230 --> 00:13:33.190
--Ow, ow, ow.
--Kotobuki,

00:13:33.190 --> 00:13:37.230
I won't be satisfied until I cut open
your pretty little chest.

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:38.520
Who are you?!

00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:40.190
Well, Kotobuki,

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:44.310
I'm Doctor Seki! You stole my job
as chief of the medical center!

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:46.600
I'll analyze every micron of your body

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:50.770
and return to those glorious days!

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:51.940
Huh?

00:13:51.940 --> 00:13:55.650
Oh, the guy who was obsessed with my body.

00:13:55.650 --> 00:13:58.350
So, this is my trauma.

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:01.690
It's true that he's the last person
I'd want to dissect me.

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:03.100
True.

00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:06.480
What?!

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:31.310
Fools!

00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:33.900
I'm the world-famous Seki!

00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:38.850
I have numerous doctorates!
My papers have been published in Future!

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:41.650
I've been on the cover of Future.

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:42.730
Me, too.

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:44.400
Ha! I won't accept it!

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:46.900
If that's true, solve this problem.

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:50.690
It's ultra-difficult,
with a zero-percent success rate!

00:14:50.690 --> 00:14:55.190
Find the radius of a circle that
intersects points A, B, C, and D.

00:14:56.690 --> 00:14:59.020
Only a genius can solve it.

00:14:59.020 --> 00:15:00.690
I'm going to do it.

00:15:00.690 --> 00:15:02.150
So will I.

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:05.600
You little brats could never figure it out!

00:15:05.600 --> 00:15:08.020
I'm going to blow your mind!

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:09.900
Then answer!

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:11.270
The answer is

00:15:11.270 --> 00:15:13.440
there is no such circle!

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:14.940
Huh? It can't be.

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:20.690
These little girls solved a problem
not even I could? In seconds?

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:22.230
No need.

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:34.270
Doctor what's-his-name
had pride, if nothing else.

00:15:34.270 --> 00:15:37.480
Pride chicken.

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:39.270
Was it that funny?

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:42.350
You sounded like a friend of mine.

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:45.940
Bravo.

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:49.100
Take care of the me in reality.

00:15:49.100 --> 00:15:50.270
All right.

00:15:50.270 --> 00:15:53.020
What should you do? Say it in words.

00:15:53.020 --> 00:15:54.270
Why?

00:15:54.270 --> 00:15:58.020
Because you always do what you say you will.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:01.770
I'll disconnect your life support.

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:04.850
Good. Sorry for a lot.

00:16:04.850 --> 00:16:07.150
You should be.

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:09.600
Thank you.

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:11.980
Kotobuki was in an Egg?

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:14.810
Yes. There can't even be a miracle now.

00:16:14.810 --> 00:16:16.690
Kotobuki is dead.

00:16:16.690 --> 00:16:20.600
Still, you're not even related.
You can't just...

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:21.940
I know.

00:16:21.940 --> 00:16:25.440
But if I delay, the government
will come for her.

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:28.310
An albino genius is a valuable sample.

00:16:28.310 --> 00:16:29.560
A sample...

00:16:29.560 --> 00:16:31.150
But that's just an excuse!

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:33.690
Can you kill a girl like her for that?

00:16:33.690 --> 00:16:38.350
She looks alive. Like she's just sleeping.

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:39.900
She's already dead.

00:16:39.900 --> 00:16:41.770
Just a container.

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:46.980
Sorry, but I can't watch.

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:51.100
It doesn't mean the same thing
as killing Seeno Evils or Haters there.

00:16:51.100 --> 00:16:53.100
Yeah! This is for real.

00:16:53.100 --> 00:16:56.310
That's too much, even if she did ask you.

00:16:56.310 --> 00:16:58.730
I can't believe you're just going to do it.

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:00.440
Then just go home.

00:17:00.440 --> 00:17:04.730
I didn't... ask you to take a field trip here.

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:06.850
You shouldn't say it like that.

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:08.650
We're worried, too.

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:09.900
About what?

00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:11.600
I mean, you're our friend.

00:17:11.600 --> 00:17:16.020
If you do that, you might end up
with trauma, or baggage, or...

00:17:16.020 --> 00:17:18.100
There's no problem, then.

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:23.400
I won't get sentimental about
stopping a dead person's respiration.

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:28.400
Oh, is that so?

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:30.100
Being smart is scary.

00:17:30.100 --> 00:17:34.810
I'm more frightened of
others' overheated passions.

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:37.730
Are you talking about me?! Are you?!

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:38.410
Hey!

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:40.060
Stop it, everyone.

00:17:40.060 --> 00:17:43.100
Kotobuki can hear you.

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:44.150
Hey.

00:17:44.150 --> 00:17:47.150
That's normal human sentimentality, right?

00:17:47.150 --> 00:17:49.480
Worrying she might hear us.

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:50.690
Ridiculous.

00:17:50.690 --> 00:17:53.150
Anyway, Neiru,

00:17:53.150 --> 00:17:56.150
you should at least sleep on it.

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:06.060
I'm going back after all.

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:07.480
Hey, Ai!

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:10.350
Ai can get close to her.

00:18:10.350 --> 00:18:15.020
She might have better luck
changing Neiru's mind alone.

00:18:15.020 --> 00:18:16.650
Well, I guess.

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:19.600
It seems like Neiru's being stubborn.

00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:21.400
Ai might get through.

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:30.850
President Aonuma is getting closer to the truth
behind the temptation of death.

00:18:30.850 --> 00:18:33.100
Kotobuki did give her a hint.

00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:35.190
Innocent sorrow.

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:39.480
You managed to deflect her
with an excuse, though.

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:41.350
Girls' suicides.

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:45.060
If we told them the real reason,
none of them would fight.

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:49.230
Yeah. Not if they knew
the root cause is the two of us.

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:50.730
Do you think so?

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:54.020
I think they would actually fight against you.

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:57.940
Because they're girls,
they understand girls' sorrows.

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:00.100
What? What's going on?

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:04.850
She's connected to Acca and Ura-Acca, too?

00:19:04.850 --> 00:19:07.230
You came to stop me?

00:19:07.230 --> 00:19:10.190
I want to hear about Kotobuki.

00:19:10.190 --> 00:19:11.520
I see.

00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:14.230
What else did Kotobuki say?

00:19:14.230 --> 00:19:15.980
What else?

00:19:15.980 --> 00:19:19.400
Why did she want you to do that for her?

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:22.350
She doesn't want adults to touch her.

00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:28.900
See? If you'd told us that, the others
would have been more understanding.

00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:30.400
Really?

00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:31.690
Yeah.

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:34.310
You're not very upfront, Neiru.

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:42.310
I really... tried to push it,

00:19:42.310 --> 00:19:44.270
but my fingers shook.

00:19:44.270 --> 00:19:46.650
Yeah.

00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:51.350
One time, Koito and I tried
fortune-telling using Kokkuri.

00:19:51.350 --> 00:19:54.770
We asked if Koito's crush liked her back.

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:57.850
I think it was probably Mr. Sawaki.

00:19:57.850 --> 00:19:58.980
Yeah.

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:01.560
The coin landed on "yes."

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:06.190
I didn't move it, so I thought Koito did,

00:20:06.190 --> 00:20:08.600
but she seemed really happy.

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:14.400
I wondered if she'd be that happy
if she'd moved it herself.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:20.020
Maybe I moved it without knowing,
to make Koito happy.

00:20:20.020 --> 00:20:23.810
But... I really don't know.

00:20:23.810 --> 00:20:26.900
That's what fantasy is.

00:20:26.900 --> 00:20:29.100
Yeah.

00:20:29.100 --> 00:20:30.520
With two of us...

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:32.190
It's fantasy.

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:37.270
Kotobuki's body was scheduled
for collection tomorrow morning.

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:39.310
Yeah.

00:20:39.310 --> 00:20:41.940
Did you want something done before that?

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:46.850
It was you who made Neiru's
Wonder Egg Kotobuki, wasn't it?

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:48.400
Just a coincidence.

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:56.400
Thank you.

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:00.810
"It is the hour to be drunken!

00:21:00.810 --> 00:21:04.310
Be drunken, if you would not
be martyred slaves of Time;

00:21:04.310 --> 00:21:06.730
be drunken continually!

00:21:06.730 --> 00:21:12.900
With wine, with poetry,
or with virtue, as you will."

00:21:12.900 --> 00:21:15.100
Let's really enjoy ourselves.

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:25.770
We only live once.

00:22:56.980 --> 00:23:01.980
Next time

00:22:58.270 --> 00:22:59.650
To be continued.
